            <div xml:id="d360">

                <pb facs="0513" n="503" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg503"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">40.00119 PW/8–1845</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The President of the Chinese Executive Yuan</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Soong</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-18">August 18, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Byrnes</hi>: In connection with what you
                    told me about Hongkong: Since Hongkong is in the China Theatre it seems to me
                    perfectly logical to say to the British that surrender of the Japanese there
                    should be tendered to the Supreme Commander of the China Theatre or his nominee,
                    leaving in abeyance the question as to the eventual disposition of Hongkong.</p>
                <p>With kind regards [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>T. V. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Soong</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
